# Multi-Tenant SEO Origin Integrity

## Context

Production inspection on 2026-07-30 confirmed that SSR metadata is being cached
with the origin of whichever request first warms a tenant/path Redis key:

- `https://thewriterco.com/` returned root metadata for
  `slushup.thewriterco.com`, while `/forum` retained `thewriterco.com`.
- `https://skaiacraft.com/` returned canonical, Open Graph, image, and favicon
  URLs rooted at `http://localhost`.
- Thread, forum, and root Open Graph URLs were HTTP even when fetched over
  HTTPS. Cloudflare rewrote eligible `href` attributes to HTTPS but did not
  rewrite Open Graph `content`, making the emitted head internally inconsistent.
- Authentication is not an SEO input. The apparent signed-in difference came
  from comparing independently warmed route keys.

The failure chain spans `backend/internal/seo`, generated nginx, tenant env
generation, and Redis invalidation:

- rendered absolute URLs are cached by client and path, without canonical origin;
- nginx overwrites `X-Forwarded-Proto` with its HTTP-side `$scheme`;
- nginx maps unknown hosts to the first tenant;
- the shared healthcheck requests `/` as `localhost` every five seconds;
- broad wildcard hosts can reach the primary SPA unless they match the narrower
  Frappe interception rule;
- production tenants do not receive an explicit `PUBLIC_BASE_URL`.

The same review also confirmed double-escaped social descriptions, ignored
`SEO.Title` and `Branding.FaviconURL`, mismatched product invalidation keys,
soft-404 behavior, and an unguarded outbound image metadata probe.

## Goal

- Make canonical, Open Graph, Twitter, image, and favicon origins deterministic,
  HTTPS, tenant-approved, and independent of request order, aliases, cookies,
  healthchecks, or hostile Host headers.
- Stop unknown/local/wildcard hosts from poisoning tenant SEO caches.
- Make cached SEO data origin-independent or explicitly origin-scoped, with
  complete mutation/config invalidation.
- Correct escaping, configured title/favicon selection, missing-route behavior,
  and image inspection safety.
- Provide a safe production rollout and purge/verification runbook for every
  tenant.

## Non-Goals

- Replacing the React SPA with full component SSR.
- Rewriting site marketing copy or choosing per-page keywords.
- Treating Cloudflare HTML rewriting as an SEO correctness mechanism.
- Automating Search Console or third-party social-crawler submissions.

## Steps

1. Add incident regression coverage before changing behavior:
   - exercise one tenant/path through approved apex, `www`, subdomain, localhost,
     forwarded-protocol, and signed/unsigned requests in different orders;
   - prove cookies/claims do not change public SEO output;
   - reproduce cross-host root cache contamination and the localhost healthcheck;
   - assert canonical, `og:url`, `og:image`, Twitter image, and favicon all use
     the same approved HTTPS origin;
   - assert apostrophes and ampersands are escaped once, not as `&amp;#39;`.
2. Define one explicit canonical origin per production tenant:
   - require and validate an absolute HTTPS `PUBLIC_BASE_URL` for production;
   - constrain its hostname to the tenant's approved `DOMAINS`;
   - generate it in `grengo new`, expose it through supported env editing, and
     preserve/validate it during import and transfer;
   - document whether `www` and other aliases redirect to the primary origin or
     serve content with a primary-origin canonical. Do not derive SEO identity
     from an arbitrary wildcard request host;
   - align `SITEMAP_BASE_URL` with the same origin instead of maintaining an
     independent default.
3. Redesign SEO caching around semantic metadata:
   - cache title, description, image reference, route state, and image metadata
     without rendered request-origin HTML, then render absolute tags using the
     current validated canonical configuration;
   - alternatively, if rendered tags remain cached, include a validated
     canonical-origin/config revision in every key and every invalidator;
   - invalidate affected entries on branding/SEO configuration changes;
   - correct forum, page, product, user, stream, and landing-route invalidation,
     including the current `/store/item/` versus `/store/product/` mismatch;
   - keep public SEO cache keys independent of authentication and rate-limit
     bypass state.
4. Harden generated nginx and health checks:
   - add a dedicated default server whose health endpoint returns success and
     whose other unknown-host requests return `444`, restoring the documented
     infrastructure contract;
   - point the shared Compose healthcheck at that endpoint instead of tenant `/`;
   - remove the host-map fallback to the first enabled tenant;
   - narrow wildcard routing to valid provisioned `site<id>` hosts or reject
     unmatched subdomains before the SPA;
   - preserve a trustworthy external scheme or consume validated proxy metadata.
     Audit Cloudflare zones for Flexible mode, Always Use HTTPS, and Automatic
     HTTPS Rewrites; prefer Full (Strict) origin TLS, while keeping SSR correctness
     independent of Cloudflare rewriting.
5. Correct metadata construction:
   - escape each raw value exactly once at the final HTML context;
   - honor `SEO.Title` for the site/default route and
     `Branding.FaviconURL` for the favicon;
   - ensure canonical and all first-party social/image URLs use the same HTTPS
     origin before Cloudflare transforms the response;
   - define image alt metadata and retain dimensions/MIME only when safely known;
   - return a real `404` or explicit `noindex` policy for missing recognized
     resources and unknown SPA paths instead of caching indexable soft 404s.
6. Secure and decouple image metadata detection:
   - reuse the repository's scrape URL validation policy to reject loopback,
     private, link-local, metadata-service, unsupported-scheme, and unsafe
     redirect destinations;
   - avoid a blocking outbound GET on every cold SSR request where dimensions
     can be captured at upload time or cached separately;
   - bound response size, redirects, MIME, dimensions, and timeout with focused
     tests.
7. Roll out with explicit incident cleanup:
   - inventory every tenant's primary origin, aliases, Cloudflare mode, and
     generated env before deployment;
   - deploy backend and regenerated nginx together;
   - purge all legacy `<client>:ssr:meta:*` keys after the new key/data contract
     is live, using scanned explicit prefixes rather than a broad Redis flush;
   - verify apex, `www`, valid subdomains, invalid subdomains, forum/thread/page/
     product routes, missing routes, and signed/unsigned requests;
   - request recrawls only after raw origin HTML and public Cloudflare HTML pass.
8. Update `.specs/caching_cdn_spec`, `.specs/infrastructure_spec`, and
   `.specs/backend_spec` with the implemented canonical-origin, host rejection,
   cache invalidation, status, and safe image-probe contracts. Record production
   verification in this todo's `.tip`.

## Verification

- `env GOCACHE=/tmp/skaia-go-cache GOTMPDIR=/tmp JWT_SECRET=test-secret go test ./internal/seo ./internal/config ./internal/forum ./internal/store`
- `go test ./internal/app/...`
- `go test ./...` from `backend/` and the root module after focused tests pass.
- Generate nginx for a fixture with multiple tenants and assert:
  - unknown hosts never select the first backend;
  - the healthcheck never requests tenant `/`;
  - only approved apex/alias and valid provisioned-site hosts route.
- Fetch raw HTML through the public CDN and, where possible, directly from the
  origin with explicit Host headers. Assert no `localhost`, unintended
  subdomain, first-tenant domain, or `http://` occurs in first-party SEO tags.
- Warm identical paths in every host/order/cookie permutation and compare the
  resulting semantic metadata and canonical origin.
- Confirm config and content mutations remove or version every affected SEO
  cache entry.
- Confirm missing resources return the chosen `404`/`noindex` contract.
- Confirm unsafe image URLs and unsafe redirect hops cause no outbound request.

